WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
A cut on your skin heals as new skin
cells are made by cell division.

2
00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:08.110
Each new cell needs a
complete copy of the DNA,

3
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.420
with an identical base sequence.

4
00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:15.880
So before every division by
mitosis, all of that DNA is copied.

5
00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:19.720
One wrong letter would be
passed on to every later copy.

6
00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:23.050
So how does the copy
come out almost perfect?

7
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:27.820
In this mission, you'll watch an enzyme
called helicase unzip the double helix

8
00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:30.590
and break the bonds between its bases.

9
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.890
Then you'll copy a short
stretch of DNA yourself,

10
00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:35.840
one base at a time.

11
00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:41.400
Your mission: find out how a cell
copies all its DNA almost perfectly.
